  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "After standard IET induction, recurrence and the Conze-Fraczek essential-value criterion, the proof must preserve reversal symmetry and track induced centers even when the ergodic IET has connections. It changes the induction center twice to rebalance high-measure thin towers and wide bases, obtaining positive-mass rigidity towers with a quantitative return bound. The new effective criterion then builds subtowers realizing an interval of essential values, while antisymmetric cancellation controls the centered linear Birkhoff sums; neither generic Rauzy-Veech induction nor the final mean-value estimate alone supplies this construction.",
